00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:12.800
bar right here and type in, "Can you connect&nbsp;
to my Roblox game?" Then find the gun tool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:24.320
in starter pack. Build a complete gun system&nbsp;
for it with raycast shooting, a reload system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:36.640
and server side damage. Body shots should deal&nbsp;
five damage and head shots should deal 20 damage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:48.640
Make the ray cast ignore accessory parts like&nbsp;
hats and hair so they don't block head shot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.360 --> 00:04:02.640
If a bullet hits any part attached to a character,&nbsp;
count it as hitting that character. Even if that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:16.400
part is inside another model, use the tools&nbsp;
activated event for firing so it works on PC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:29.760
mobile, and console. Keep the fire rate check on&nbsp;
the server, but give it a small tolerance for lag.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:41.520
So legitimate shots are never silently rejected&nbsp;
and only play the gunshot effects when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:54.960
server confirms the shot. Add a bullet tracer for&nbsp;
every shot that every player in the game can see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:09.280
Every shot must also push the camera up slightly&nbsp;
like real gun recoil. Do not skip this. Play the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:22.720
sound named fire inside the tools handle every&nbsp;
time the gun shoots. Create a screen GUI that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:34.000
shows the current ammo out of the magazine size&nbsp;
and update it when the player fires and reloads.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:45.440
The gun should reload when the player presses R&nbsp;
on their keyboard and also when the player taps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:55.200
or clicks the ammo counter. So it works on&nbsp;
mobile too. Inside the config in the tool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:06.000
create number values named damage,&nbsp;
headshot damage, fire rate, reload time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:15.840
and magazine size. Where fire rate means the&nbsp;
number of seconds between shots, and make every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:26.880
script read from those values. So, the gun can&nbsp;
be customized without touching any code. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:46.000
going to speed this part up. Just make sure you&nbsp;
click allow whenever Claude asks for permission.

